{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"schanuel s lemma schanuel s lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md","fileName":"Schanuel's Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Schanuel's Lemma","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Projective Flat and Injective Modules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Projective Resolution","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"schanuel s lemma schanuel s lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md","fileName":"Schanuel's Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Schanuel's Lemma","heading":"Schanuel's Lemma","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Schanuel's lemma compares two projective presentations of the same module. If P/M and P′/M′ are isomorphic with P and P′ projective, then P ⊕ M′ is isomorphic to P′ ⊕ M.\n\nThe lemma shows that kernels of different projective presentations are stably equivalent. It supports the independence of invariants derived from a chosen [[Projective Resolution]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Projective Resolution","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"schanuel s lemma schanuel s lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Schanuel's Lemma.md","fileName":"Schanuel's Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Schanuel's Lem